    "level": "b1",
    "unit": 23,
    "title": "Too / Enough",
    "title_ko": "Too / Enough (충분함 표현)",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "'Too + adjective' means more than necessary, usually with a negative result: 'too expensive'. 'Enough' means a sufficient amount and comes after adjectives ('good enough') but before nouns ('enough time'). Both are often followed by 'to + verb': 'too tired to walk', 'old enough to drive'.",
    "explanation_ko": "'too + 형용사'는 필요 이상이라는 뜻이며 보통 부정적 결과를 동반합니다: 'too expensive'. 'enough'는 충분한 양을 나타내며 형용사 뒤('good enough'), 명사 앞('enough time')에 옵니다. 둘 다 'to + 동사'와 자주 함께 쓰입니다: 'too tired to walk', 'old enough to drive'.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "This coffee is too hot to drink.",
        "ko": "이 커피는 너무 뜨거워서 못 마셔요."
      },
      {
        "en": "I don't have enough time today.",
        "ko": "저는 오늘 시간이 충분하지 않아요."
      },
      {
        "en": "She's old enough to travel alone.",
        "ko": "그녀는 혼자 여행할 만큼 나이가 됐어요."
      }
    ]
  },
  "tasks": [
